      "message": "On floss, the flag_enabled always evaluates to false, so we return early here, which is not what we want.\n\nCan we do the reverse instead? i.e.\n```\nif (IS_FLAG_ENABLED(smp_tx_complete_callback)) {\n  return;\n}\n```\n\nSo the flag is automatically on, and on Android we need to explicitly turn it off to execute the current flow.\n\nOr is there a better way to do it?",
